    "summary": "I built a single-column tower three storeys tall from north-half hex bases. A base can only stack on the same kind of base, and drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base, so all three storeys are half bases. The bottom storey has a drawer and the top storey has an open bin split into two compartments, with no cover over it. The middle storey's open faces, including its cut face, are closed with end caps. I capped the open faces and ran lockJoints, which said there were no joints to bolt. check_build reports no issues and the mesh-collision check came back clear. I didn't add props because the brief doesn't describe a use. It comes to 25 parts, about 1446 g of filament and 2053 minutes of printing.",
    "outcome": "built"
  },
